Atomic Multi-Chain Commit Protocol (high level)
Plan: Strategy compiles into an atomic plan: [op1@chainA, op2@chainB, op3@chainC].

Simulate: Sidecar(s) simulate execution across all targeted chains. Produce receipts for each simulated leg.

Lock: For local-chain or partner chains that support locks, attempt pre-lock (e.g., reserve funds on chain, use HTLC or deposit in cross-chain escrow). If any pre-lock fails abort.

Execute:

If all pre-locks succeed, broadcast the plan to executors:

For chains with proofs: submit operator txs and return proofs.

For external chains that don't support atomic proofs: execute best-effort and prepare rollbacks.

Verify: Collect on-chain proofs for each leg; verify using UNIVERSAL_VERIFY(proof).

Commit: If all legs verified, commit atomic outcome on Atlas Sphere by writing final states (e.g., finalize swap receipts, distribute fees).

Revert: If any leg fails verification, run compensating transactions (refund) in the reverse order using guaranteed failsafes encoded in plan. Receipt-based atomicity ensures proofs are tamper-proof.

Important: For chains that can’t produce on-demand succinct proofs, use escrow/lock/HTLC-style fallback; these are not fully atomic but allow safe rollbacks.

